WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.043
Most new ideas are bad.

00:00:02.043 --> 00:00:04.320
There’s a reason&nbsp;people haven’t done it before.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.876
Just like most mutations are 
evolutionary dead&nbsp;ends.

00:00:08.876 --> 00:00:14.565
The thing about capitalism is 
that it is an emergent system.

00:00:14.565 --> 00:00:16.836
Like all&nbsp;evolutionary mechanisms,

00:00:16.836 --> 00:00:19.436
powered by mutations.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.588
And in this case, what the&nbsp;
mutations are

00:00:23.588 --> 00:00:26.623
are very weird people

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.455
trying new stuff.

00:00:28.455 --> 00:00:32.889
And when we need really big&nbsp;
progress, big new stuff,

00:00:32.889 --> 00:00:36.114
that means we need really, really weird people.

00:00:36.114 --> 00:00:39.393
I'm not saying that&nbsp;every weirdo has

00:00:39.393 --> 00:00:42.182
a brilliant apocalypse-averting idea

00:00:42.182 --> 00:00:45.890
that also happens to be 
a viable commercial&nbsp;enterprise.

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:50.734
The way forward is to figure out what the public 
and private sector can each do best

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:53.300
and&nbsp;help them figure out how to stay in their lane.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:57.456
Weirdos trying stuff and sometimes 
being allowed&nbsp;to fail at it

00:00:57.456 --> 00:00:59.601
are our best hope as a species.

